      "message": "I\u0027m not sure what you meant by \u0027run off to\u0027 or \u0027bad proxy\u0027. There are only two zones: 13 \u003c angle \u003c 180 and 180 \u003c angle \u003c 373. For EC to recognize a valid mode, the lid angle has to stay in either of the zones consistently.\n\nPreviously, there are two functions. They\u0027re mutually exclusive. When one returns false, the other returns true and vice versa. It means we just need to call one of the functions. If the results are mixed (front and back), lid_angle_update is no-op.",
